# User-facing copy

Every string a person reads must be grammatically correct in the language it is written in. That includes accents, agreement, punctuation, and spelling.

This covers UI labels, locale files, emails, PDFs, empty states, errors, and buttons.

```text
Bad:  El proceso termino. Si hace falta alguna aclaracion, te contactaremos.
Good: El proceso terminó. Si hace falta alguna aclaración, te contactaremos.
```

Match the language already used on that surface. Do not leave a new string in a worse form than the surrounding copy.
